/-!
# Section 5: the gadget template chains (data)

**Generated by a program that is not included in this repository.**

For every unit kind the template chain (boundary order, from the first vertex after the
corridor corner `c1` to the last vertex before `d1`) in integer template coordinates: the template
point `T` of `docs/section5/07_template_vertices.md` is `tmplV k = D · T` with `D = tmplD k`.
These are literally the lists `Tmpl.addGEV`, `Tmpl.addLEV`, `Tmpl.addORV`, `Tmpl.invV` of
`Templates/*Data.lean` (with the same denominators `addGED`, …); the bridge lemmas are
`tmplV_ge` … in `Assemble/Sep.lean`.  The data is duplicated here so that the construction does not depend on
the certificate files.

Also the receiver segments: `tmplT k` lists the template left endpoints `T_τ` of the receivers
(index `τ`; `τ = 0` belongs to the largest working slot), as used by the corridor.
-/

@[expose] public section

